| `tests/integration/test_swallowed_error_gate.py` | Fails a bare `except:`, and a broad handler that only drops the error, unless its `# noqa: BLE001` or `E722` gives a reason, and fails every such suppression whose reason is blank, so a caller never reads a thrown-away failure as a success; through `scripts/expiring_tier.py` it fails a narrow handler that only drops the error or puts a fixed value in its place, `contextlib.suppress(...)` and `ignore_errors=True` unless a `# noqa: DROP001`, `DROP002` or `DROP003` gives a reason. | `make test` | — | It cannot see a handler that does work but never looks at the error. Not the lint rule itself: ruff's BLE001 and E722 run under `make lint`. | [python-style.md](../guides/python-style.md) | always |
